{#
  ============================================================================
  HYPER · PRODUCTS HIGHLIGHT  ·  أبرز المنتجات
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ┌──────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┐
    │  HOT ITEMS               │   ┌──────────────────────┐     │
    │  Shop The Winter Set     │   │    ┌────────────┐    │     │
    │  a line of copy…         │   │    │  product   │    │     │
    │  ( Shop Now › )          │   │    │   shot     │    │     │
    │                          │   │    └────────────┘    │     │
    │  ▢ name · price · ○      │   └──────────────────────┘     │
    │  2/2 ──────── ‹ ›        │                                │
    └──────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────┘

  Styled in assets/style.css → "15.13 PRODUCTS HIGHLIGHT", where the measured
  numbers and the one derived one are written down.

  ── Only the card slides ──
  Measured across the reference recording, the eyebrow, the heading, the copy
  and the button never change — their pixel diff is flat 0.0 except while the
  page is scrolling. Only the small product card and its pager move, and they
  move on a CLICK (each change lands on an arrow press, never on a timer). So
  there is no autoplay here and the copy is not per-slide.

  ── Why `products` is a widget-level picker and there are no blocks ──
  A `products` picker inside a `blocks` entry stops the Theme Editor rendering
  that block's settings at all — the previous widget in this folder carried
  that warning and it still holds. One product per slide, read straight off the
  widget-level list, needs no blocks and cannot hit it.

  ── What the reference has and this does not ──
  Its big media is a VIDEO with play/mute controls. Qumra has no `video`
  setting type and nothing in this theme ships one, so this takes an image and
  the controls are dropped rather than faked.
  ============================================================================
#}

{% set id = widget.id %}
{% set d = widget.data %}

{% set eyebrow   = d.eyebrow | default('') %}
{% set title     = d.title | default('') %}
{% set body      = d.body | default('') %}
{% set ctaText   = d.cta_text | default('') %}
{% set ctaUrl    = d.cta_url | default('/shop') %}
{% set mediaPos  = d.media_position | default('end') %}
{% set mediaImg  = d.media_image %}
{% set shotImg   = d.shot_image %}
{% set products  = d.products | default([]) %}
{% set count     = products | length %}
{% set showShot  = d.show_shot | default(true) %}
{% set mediaW    = d.media_width | default(52) %}
{% set mediaH    = d.media_height | default(105) %}
{% set gapW      = d.column_gap | default(6) %}

{# A `media` setting arrives as an object on some stores and a bare string on
   others — the same shape offer-cards already normalises. #}
{% macro mediaUrl(m) %}{% if m %}{% if m is string %}{{ m }}{% elif m.fileUrl %}{{ m.fileUrl }}{% elif m.url %}{{ m.url }}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

{# ⚠️  `| length`, not truthiness: a macro returns a SafeString OBJECT, and an
   object is truthy even when it holds an empty string. #}
{% set mediaSrc = mediaUrl(mediaImg) | trim %}
{# Demo picture while the field is empty: assets/demo-*.jpg are CC0 photos
   (sources in _ref/demo-images-sources.txt). An uploaded image replaces it. #}
{% set mediaIsDemo = (mediaSrc | length) == 0 %}
{% set mediaSrc = mediaSrc if (mediaSrc | length) else ('demo-highlight.jpg' | assets) %}
{% set shotSrc  = mediaUrl(shotImg)  | trim %}
{# The demo shot comes WITH the demo backdrop, as a pair. Over the merchant's
   own photograph an empty shot keeps its "add a shot" skeleton below — a stock
   picture laid on their picture would be worse than the prompt. #}
{% set shotSrc = shotSrc if ((shotSrc | length) or not mediaIsDemo) else ('demo-shot.jpg' | assets) %}
{% set hasMedia = (mediaSrc | length) > 0 %}
{% set hasShot  = (shotSrc  | length) > 0 %}

{# ---- is it a clip? ----
   Both frames in the reference are VIDEO — measured frame to frame with the
   page still, the media peaks at 209–255 against a static-text noise floor of
   4, and the inset moves MORE than the backdrop. Qumra has no `video` setting
   type, only `media` (documented as «صورة/وسائط»), so the file itself is what
   says which it is and the picker stays one field either way.

   ⚠️  `indexOf`, chained — NOT a flag set inside a `{% for %}` over an
   extension list. Nunjucks scopes `{% set %}` to the block it runs in, so that
   flag reads back as its pre-loop value and every clip silently renders as a
   broken <img>. Same trap the product card documents for its badges. #}
{% set mLow = mediaSrc | lower %}
{% set sLow = shotSrc | lower %}
{% set mediaIsClip = mLow.indexOf('.mp4') > -1 or mLow.indexOf('.webm') > -1 or mLow.indexOf('.mov') > -1 or mLow.indexOf('.m4v') > -1 or mLow.indexOf('.ogv') > -1 %}
{% set shotIsClip  = sLow.indexOf('.mp4') > -1 or sLow.indexOf('.webm') > -1 or sLow.indexOf('.mov') > -1 or sLow.indexOf('.m4v') > -1 or sLow.indexOf('.ogv') > -1 %}

{# `playsinline` is what stops iOS taking the clip fullscreen, and `muted` is
   what lets it autoplay at all — every browser blocks an unmuted autoplay.
   Decorative, so no controls and no audio track is expected. #}
{% macro frame(src, isClip, alt) %}{% if isClip %}<video src="{{ src }}" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" aria-hidden="true"></video>{% else %}<img src="{{ src }}" alt="{{ alt }}" loading="lazy"/>{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

{# The editor-facing hint. Inert and aria-hidden like every other skeleton in
   this theme — see style.css → "15.29.1 EMPTY-SECTION SKELETON". #}
{% macro phHint() %}<span class="hy-ph-hint"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>{{ t('common.placeholder_add') }}</span>{% endmacro %}

{% macro arrow(dir) %}<svg class="rtl-flip" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="{{ 'M15 6 9 12l6 6' if dir == 'prev' else 'm9 6 6 6-6 6' }}"/></svg>{% endmacro %}

<section id="hy-hl-{{ id }}"
         class="hy-hl {{ 'hy-hl--start' if mediaPos == 'start' }}"
         x-data="{
           i: 0,
           n: {{ count if count > 0 else 1 }},
           prev() { this.i = (this.i - 1 + this.n) % this.n },
           next() { this.i = (this.i + 1) % this.n }
         }">

  <div class="hy-hl-inner">

    {# ---------- copy ---------- #}
    <div class="hy-hl-copy">
      {% if eyebrow %}<p class="hy-hl-eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if title %}<h2 class="hy-hl-title">{{ title }}</h2>{% endif %}
      {% if body %}<p class="hy-hl-text">{{ body }}</p>{% endif %}

      {% if ctaText %}
        <div class="hy-hl-cta">
          <a href="{{ ctaUrl }}" class="hy-btn hy-btn--solid hy-btn--pill hy-btn--arrow">
            <span>{{ ctaText }}</span>
            <i class="hy-btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="rtl-flip" width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                   stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg>
            </i>
          </a>
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if count == 0 %}
        {# The real row at its real size, in grey: the shape says "a picture, a
           name, a price and a way to buy" before anything is chosen. #}
        <div class="hy-hl-slider" data-hy-auto-hl>
          <div class="hy-hl-slides">
            <article class="hy-hl-slide is-active" data-hy-placeholder aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="hy-hl-thumb hy-ph-box"></span>
              <div class="hy-hl-info">
                <span class="hy-ph-line" style="--ph-line-w: 62%;"></span>
                <span class="hy-ph-line" style="--ph-line-w: 34%; --ph-line-h: 10px;"></span>
              </div>
              <span class="hy-hl-atc hy-ph-box"></span>
            </article>
          </div>
          <div class="hy-hl-pager">{{ phHint() }}</div>
        </div>

      {% else %}
        <div class="hy-hl-slider">
          {# Every slide occupies the same grid cell, so the block keeps the
             height of the TALLEST product name and the pager under it does not
             jump when a longer one comes round. #}
          <div class="hy-hl-slides">
            {% for p in products %}
              {% set price = p.pricing.price | default(0) %}
              {% set was   = p.pricing.compareAtPrice | default(0) %}
              {% set onSale = was and was > price %}
              {% set url = '/products/' ~ (p.slug | default(p.handle) | default(p._id)) %}
              {# Same two tests split-slider and ui/cart.njk use, and for the same
                 reason they give: a product with options CANNOT be added blind.
                 `CartManager.add(id, 1)` posts no `options`, so the server files
                 it with no variant, at the PARENT price — which is how one cart
                 ended up with two "بعضل" rows, identical but for a price, one of
                 them a variant and one of them not. #}
              {% set inStock = p.allowBackorder or (not p.trackQuantity) or p.variantsCount or (p.options | default([], true) | length) > 0 or (p.quantity | default(0, true)) > 0 %}
              {% set hasVariants = (p.variantsCount and p.variantsCount > 0) or (p.options and (p.options | length) > 0) %}

              <article class="hy-hl-slide {{ 'is-active' if loop.index0 == 0 }}"
                       :class="{ 'is-active': i === {{ loop.index0 }} }"
                       {% if count > 1 %}:aria-hidden="i === {{ loop.index0 }} ? 'false' : 'true'"{% endif %}>

                <a href="{{ url }}" class="hy-hl-thumb" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                  {% if p.images and p.images[0] and p.images[0].fileUrl %}
                    <img src="{{ p.images[0].fileUrl }}" alt="" loading="lazy"/>
                  {% endif %}
                </a>

                <div class="hy-hl-info">
                  <a href="{{ url }}" class="hy-hl-name">{{ p.title }}</a>
                  <div class="hy-hl-money">
                    {# `| money` and never a hand-rolled division — prices cross
                       this boundary in minor units. #}
                    <span class="hy-price {{ 'hy-price--sale' if onSale }}">{% if price == 0 %}{{ t('common.free') }}{% else %}{{ price | money }}{% endif %}</span>
                    {% if onSale %}<span class="hy-price-was">{{ was | money }}</span>{% endif %}
                  </div>

                  {# The shared swatch component, so this row and the catalog
                     card can never drift apart. Image swatches only — that is
                     what the option payload carries. #}
                  {% if (p.options | default([]) | length) > 0 %}
                    <div class="hy-pcard-swatches" aria-hidden="true">
                      {% for o in p.options %}
                        {% for v in (o.values | default([])) %}
                          {% if v.image and v.image.fileUrl %}
                            <span class="hy-pcard-swatch" title="{{ v.label }}">
                              <img src="{{ v.image.fileUrl }}" alt="" loading="lazy"/>
                            </span>
                          {% endif %}
                        {% endfor %}
                      {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                  {% endif %}
                </div>

                {% set cartIcon %}<svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                       stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="M2.2 2.8h3l2.2 11a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.7 1.4h8.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.7-1.4l1.5-7.5H6.2"/><circle cx="9.4" cy="20" r="1.4"/><circle cx="18" cy="20" r="1.4"/>
                  </svg>{% endset %}

                {% if inStock and not hasVariants %}
                  {# `_id`, not the handle — CartManager takes the id. #}
                  <button type="button"
                          class="hy-hl-atc"
                          onclick="CartManager.add('{{ p._id }}', 1)"
                          aria-label="{{ t('pages.product.add_to_cart') }}">{{ cartIcon }}</button>
                {% else %}
                  <a href="{{ url }}" class="hy-hl-atc"
                     aria-label="{{ t('products.shop') if hasVariants else t('pages.product.out_of_stock') }}">{{ cartIcon }}</a>
                {% endif %}
              </article>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>

          {% if count > 1 %}
            <div class="hy-hl-pager">
              {# Forced LTR in the CSS — 2/2 is a fraction, not a phrase. #}
              <span class="hy-hl-count"><span x-text="i + 1">1</span>/{{ count }}</span>
              <span class="hy-hl-line" aria-hidden="true">
                <span :style="'width: ' + ((i + 1) / n * 100) + '%'" style="width: {{ (100 / count) | round }}%;"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="hy-hl-arrows">
                <button type="button" class="hy-hl-arrow" @click="prev()" aria-label="{{ t('common.prev') }}">{{ arrow('prev') }}</button>
                <button type="button" class="hy-hl-arrow" @click="next()" aria-label="{{ t('common.next') }}">{{ arrow('next') }}</button>
              </span>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {# ---------- media ---------- #}
    <div class="hy-hl-media {{ 'hy-ph-box' if not hasMedia }}"
         {% if not hasMedia %}data-hy-placeholder aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}>

      {% if hasMedia %}{{ frame(mediaSrc, mediaIsClip, title) }}{% endif %}

      {# One message per empty area, not two: with no big image the whole frame
         is already a skeleton carrying the hint, and a second dashed box
         floating inside it reads as damage rather than as an invitation. #}
      {% if showShot %}
        {% if hasShot %}
          <span class="hy-hl-shot">{{ frame(shotSrc, shotIsClip, '') }}</span>
        {# Not over the demo picture: an empty dashed box on a stock photo reads as
           a broken page, not as an invitation to add a shot. #}
        {% elif hasMedia and not mediaIsDemo %}
          <span class="hy-hl-shot hy-ph-box" data-hy-placeholder aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {% endif %}
      {% endif %}

      {% if not hasMedia %}{{ phHint() }}{% endif %}
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{% if count == 0 %}
<script>
  /* ---- nothing picked: borrow the store's products ----
     HayatAuto (main.js) hands over the next few products, and the slider is
     built from them with the same markup as the server loop above (swatches
     aside — the list payload has no options). The cart button starts as a link
     and only becomes "add" once the FULL record shows no options: one added
     blind lands in the cart with no variant, at the parent price. */
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('hy-hl-{{ id }}');
    if (!root) return;
    var WANT = 3;
    var L = {
      add: {{ t('pages.product.add_to_cart') | dump | safe }},
      shop: {{ t('products.shop') | dump | safe }},
      out: {{ t('pages.product.out_of_stock') | dump | safe }},
      free: {{ t('common.free') | dump | safe }},
      prev: {{ t('common.prev') | dump | safe }},
      next: {{ t('common.next') | dump | safe }}
    };
    /* Same glyph as `cartIcon` in the loop above (the header's cart) — that one is scoped to it. */
    var cart = '<svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.2 2.8h3l2.2 11a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.7 1.4h8.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.7-1.4l1.5-7.5H6.2"/><circle cx="9.4" cy="20" r="1.4"/><circle cx="18" cy="20" r="1.4"/></svg>';
    /* The `arrow()` macro, written out: a macro returns a SafeString OBJECT, and
       `| dump` serialises the object — the arrows rendered "[object Object]". */
    var svg = function (d) { return '<svg class="rtl-flip" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="' + d + '"/></svg>'; };
    var arrPrev = svg('M15 6 9 12l6 6');
    var arrNext = svg('m9 6 6 6-6 6');

    function slide(p, k, n) {
      var A = window.HayatAuto, esc = HayatCard.esc, url = A.url(p), img = A.img(p);
      var price = (p.pricing && p.pricing.price) || 0, was = (p.pricing && p.pricing.compareAtPrice) || 0;
      var sale = was && was > price;
      return '<article class="hy-hl-slide' + (k === 0 ? ' is-active' : '') + '" :class="{ \'is-active\': i === ' + k + ' }"' +
          (n > 1 ? ' :aria-hidden="i === ' + k + ' ? \'false\' : \'true\'"' : '') + '>' +
        '<a href="' + url + '" class="hy-hl-thumb" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">' +
          (img ? '<img src="' + esc(img) + '" alt="" loading="lazy"/>' : '') + '</a>' +
        '<div class="hy-hl-info">' +
          '<a href="' + url + '" class="hy-hl-name">' + esc(p.title) + '</a>' +
          '<div class="hy-hl-money">' +
            '<span class="hy-price' + (sale ? ' hy-price--sale' : '') + '">' + esc(price ? window.formatMoney(price) : L.free) + '</span>' +
            (sale ? '<span class="hy-price-was">' + esc(window.formatMoney(was)) + '</span>' : '') +
          '</div>' +
        '</div>' +
        '<a href="' + url + '" class="hy-hl-atc" aria-label="' + esc(L.shop) + '">' + cart + '</a>' +
      '</article>';
    }

    function pager(n) {
      if (n < 2) return '';
      return '<div class="hy-hl-pager">' +
        '<span class="hy-hl-count"><span x-text="i + 1">1</span>/' + n + '</span>' +
        '<span class="hy-hl-line" aria-hidden="true"><span :style="\'width: \' + ((i + 1) / n * 100) + \'%\'" style="width: ' + Math.round(100 / n) + '%;"></span></span>' +
        '<span class="hy-hl-arrows">' +
          '<button type="button" class="hy-hl-arrow" @click="prev()" aria-label="' + HayatCard.esc(L.prev) + '">' + arrPrev + '</button>' +
          '<button type="button" class="hy-hl-arrow" @click="next()" aria-label="' + HayatCard.esc(L.next) + '">' + arrNext + '</button>' +
        '</span></div>';
    }

    function fill() {
      var box = root.querySelector('[data-hy-auto-hl]');
      if (!box || !window.HayatAuto) return;
      HayatAuto.take(WANT).then(function (list) {
        if (!list.length) return;                /* skeleton stays */
        if (window.Alpine) { var st = Alpine.$data(root); st.i = 0; st.n = list.length; }
        box.innerHTML = '<div class="hy-hl-slides">' +
          list.map(function (p, k) { return slide(p, k, list.length); }).join('') +
          '</div>' + pager(list.length);

        var atcs = box.querySelectorAll('.hy-hl-atc');
        list.forEach(function (p, k) {
          HayatAuto.full(p).then(function (full) {
            var a = atcs[k];
            if (!a) return;
            if (!HayatAuto.inStock(full)) { a.setAttribute('aria-label', L.out); return; }
            if (HayatAuto.hasOptions(full)) return;
            var btn = document.createElement('button');
            btn.type = 'button';
            btn.className = 'hy-hl-atc';
            btn.setAttribute('aria-label', L.add);
            btn.innerHTML = cart;
            btn.addEventListener('click', function () { CartManager.add(full._id || p._id, 1); });
            a.replaceWith(btn);
          });
        });
      });
    }
    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', fill);
    } else {
      fill();
    }
  })();
</script>
{% endif %}

{% if (hasMedia and mediaIsClip) or (hasShot and shotIsClip) %}
<script>
  /* `prefers-reduced-motion` cannot reach an autoplaying <video> from CSS, and
     a looping clip is exactly the kind of motion that rule exists for. First
     frame still shows — it is paused, not removed. */
  (function () {
    if (!document.documentElement.classList.contains('hy-no-motion') && (!window.matchMedia || !window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches)) return;
    var root = document.getElementById('hy-hl-{{ id }}');
    if (!root) return;
    [].forEach.call(root.querySelectorAll('video'), function (v) {
      v.autoplay = false;
      v.removeAttribute('autoplay');
      v.pause();
    });
  })();
</script>
{% endif %}

{# Shape knob. The `-set` suffix is load-bearing: this block is an ID selector,
   so a plain `--hy-hl-media` would beat the stylesheet's responsive rules and a
   merchant's desktop split would survive into a 390px viewport. #}
<style>
  #hy-hl-{{ id }} { --hy-hl-media-set: {{ mediaW }}%; --hy-hl-h-set: {{ mediaH }}; --hy-hl-gap-set: {{ gapW }}%; }
</style>

{# Per-section palette. Emits nothing unless `colors_enabled` is on, so the
   switch IS the revert. Must stay last — see the partial's header for why. #}
{% ui "section-colors.njk", scope='#hy-hl-' ~ id, c=d %}
